# Credentials — NEVER commit
credentials.toml*

# Databento job artifacts.
#
# The PAYLOADS stay ignored (hundreds of GB of .dbn.zst). The RECEIPTS do not:
# manifest/condition/metadata .json are PROVIDER receipts -- they carry the per-file
# SHA-256 checksums and the acquisition provenance, and they are NOT locally
# regenerable. Re-deriving one means re-downloading from Databento.
#
# The blanket `jobs/` rule was written to exclude payloads and took the receipts with
# it. Measured 2026-08-14: 34 receipts / 1.5 MB, all nlink=1 and in NO git object --
# including the 147,197 B GLBX manifest a previous session spent its effort rescuing
# from a script that would have atomically overwritten it.
#
# Secret-scanned before un-ignoring: 0 hits for api_key/token/secret/bearer/password;
# every 28+ char string is a 64-hex SHA-256; URLs are api.databento.com batch-download
# paths with NO query strings, so no credential is embedded. `credentials.toml*` stays
# ignored by its own rule at line 2 and is unaffected by anything below.
jobs/*
!jobs/*/
jobs/*/*
!jobs/*/manifest.json
!jobs/*/condition.json
!jobs/*/metadata.json

# Virtual environment
.venv/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# macOS metadata
.DS_Store

# Download output (can be hundreds of GB)
data/

# Python build artifacts
dist/
build/
